The sum of the first \(n\) terms of a geometric sequence is \(S_n = a \frac{1 - r^n}{1 - r}\), where \(a = \frac{1}{3}\) and \(r = \frac{1}{3}\).  
For \(n = 5\):  
\[
S_5 = \frac{1}{3} \cdot \frac{1 - (\frac{1}{3})^5}{1 - \frac{1}{3}} 
= \frac{1}{3} \cdot \frac{1 - \frac{1}{243}}{\frac{2}{3}} 
= \frac{1}{3} \cdot \frac{242}{243} \cdot \frac{3}{2} 
= \frac{242}{486} 
= \frac{121}{243}.
\]  
So the sum is \(\frac{121}{243}\).

